WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.942
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level four.

2
00:00:06.242 --> 00:00:09.814
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.114 --> 00:00:17.039
Unit nine: Global Health Diplomacy. Today you will add emphasis by fronting adjectives and phrases with inversion.

4
00:00:17.339 --> 00:00:19.922
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:24.274
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:26.536
Pandemic response.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:32.684
Pandemic response means the actions governments take to control a disease that spreads worldwide.

8
00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:35.840
A fast pandemic response saved many lives.

9
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.613
Your turn. Say: Pandemic response.

10
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.060
Pandemic response.

11
00:00:44.817 --> 00:00:46.421
Vaccine distribution.

12
00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:52.435
Vaccine distribution means the process of delivering vaccines to people in different places.

13
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.071
Fair vaccine distribution reaches rural clinics.

14
00:00:56.683 --> 00:01:00.009
Your turn. Say: Vaccine distribution.

15
00:01:02.867 --> 00:01:04.820
Vaccine distribution.

16
00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:07.409
World Health Organization.

17
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:13.737
World Health Organization means the United Nations agency that leads international health work.

18
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.708
The World Health Organization issued new guidelines.

19
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:21.712
Your turn. Say: World Health Organization.

20
00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.404
World Health Organization.

21
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.476
Health emergency.

22
00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:33.689
Health emergency means a sudden, serious danger to the health of many people.

23
00:01:34.283 --> 00:01:36.573
The government declared a health emergency.

24
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:40.242
Your turn. Say: Health emergency.

25
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.914
Health emergency.

26
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.185
Cross-border outbreak.

27
00:01:48.183 --> 00:01:52.784
Cross-border outbreak means a sudden spread of disease from one country into others.

28
00:01:53.383 --> 00:01:56.590
A cross-border outbreak closed several airports.

29
00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.300
Your turn. Say: Cross-border outbreak.

30
00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:05.445
Cross-border outbreak.

31
00:02:06.183 --> 00:02:07.695
Global health equity.

32
00:02:08.683 --> 00:02:13.458
Global health equity means fair access to health care for people in every country.

33
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.141
Global health equity remains an unfinished goal.

34
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.482
Your turn. Say: Global health equity.

35
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:25.996
Global health equity.

36
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.285
Disease surveillance.

37
00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:34.069
Disease surveillance means the careful tracking of illnesses to spot outbreaks early.

38
00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:37.693
Disease surveillance detected the virus within days.

39
00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:41.679
Your turn. Say: Disease surveillance.

40
00:02:44.533 --> 00:02:46.231
Disease surveillance.

41
00:02:46.983 --> 00:02:48.460
International aid.

42
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:53.505
International aid means money and help given by countries to others in need.

43
00:02:54.117 --> 00:02:56.685
International aid paid for new clinics.

44
00:02:57.283 --> 00:03:00.087
Your turn. Say: International aid.

45
00:03:02.933 --> 00:03:04.364
International aid.

46
00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:08.922
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:09.783 --> 00:03:16.279
Visal, a report says 'Particularly worrying is the gap in vaccine distribution.' Why is 'is' before 'the gap'?

48
00:03:17.383 --> 00:03:29.976
That is fronting with inversion. The adjective or phrase moves to the start for emphasis, then the verb comes before its subject. Normal order: The gap is particularly worrying.

49
00:03:31.083 --> 00:03:33.176
Is it only with adjectives?

50
00:03:34.283 --> 00:03:47.538
No. 'Of greatest concern are cross-border outbreaks' and 'Among the main tasks is disease surveillance' also work. The structure suits formal reports and speeches.

51
00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.464
How do I choose the verb form?

52
00:03:51.550 --> 00:04:01.096
The verb agrees with the real subject after it: 'Most urgent is the need' but 'Most urgent are the needs of poor countries'.

53
00:04:02.233 --> 00:04:03.687
Part three: grammar.

54
00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:09.998
Grammar focus: Fronting plus inversion: Adjective plus be plus subject.

55
00:04:10.298 --> 00:04:11.519
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:12.217 --> 00:04:15.458
Particularly worrying is the gap in vaccine distribution.

57
00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:20.428
Of greatest concern are cross-border outbreaks of new diseases.

58
00:04:21.317 --> 00:04:24.373
Among the main tasks is reliable disease surveillance.

59
00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:34.069
Move an adjective or phrase to the start for emphasis, then put be before the subject. Make be agree with the real subject: …is the gap / …are the needs.

60
00:04:34.817 --> 00:04:38.688
Be careful! Don't say: Particularly worrying the gap is.

61
00:04:40.633 --> 00:04:43.318
Say: Particularly worrying is the gap.

62
00:04:43.618 --> 00:04:45.281
Put the verb before the subject.

63
00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.545
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:51.263
When Disease Crosses Borders.

65
00:04:51.563 --> 00:04:55.467
A health emergency in one country can quickly become a global concern.

66
00:04:56.467 --> 00:05:02.147
Central to any pandemic response is disease surveillance, which spots a cross-border outbreak early.

67
00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:08.895
Equally important is fair vaccine distribution, because global health equity protects everyone.

68
00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:15.139
Leading the coordination is the World Health Organization, which advises governments and shares data.

69
00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:20.513
Vital, too, is international aid for countries whose health systems are weak.

70
00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:25.869
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:26.717 --> 00:05:29.819
Particularly serious blank the shortage of vaccines.

72
00:05:30.119 --> 00:05:32.925
A, is. B, are. C, does.

73
00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:37.909
The answer is A: is.

74
00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:42.849
The organisation that leads global health cooperation is the blank.

75
00:05:43.149 --> 00:05:47.789
A, Summit. B, World Health Organization. C, Trade Bloc.

76
00:05:51.333 --> 00:05:54.564
The answer is B: World Health Organization.

77
00:05:55.717 --> 00:05:57.391
Choose the correct sentence.

78
00:05:57.691 --> 00:06:04.932
A, Most urgent is the need for aid.. B, Most urgent the need is for aid.. C, Most urgent need is the for aid..

79
00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:11.430
The answer is A: Most urgent is the need for aid..

80
00:06:12.583 --> 00:06:16.290
Fair access to health care for all countries is global health blank.

81
00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:20.406
A, debt. B, equity. C, militarization.

82
00:06:23.967 --> 00:06:26.001
The answer is B: equity.

83
00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.334
According to the reading, what spots an outbreak early?

84
00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:35.204
A, border policy. B, tariffs. C, disease surveillance.

85
00:06:38.767 --> 00:06:41.265
The answer is C: disease surveillance.

86
00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:45.781
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:46.617 --> 00:06:51.484
Why is international cooperation especially important during a global pandemic?

88
00:07:00.283 --> 00:07:01.644
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:01.944 --> 00:07:31.270
A pandemic crosses borders faster than any government can stop it, so one country's failure can threaten everyone. Cooperation lets nations share data on disease surveillance, develop vaccines together and distribute them fairly. Without global health equity, new variants can appear in poorly protected regions and return. Working together is therefore both the ethical and the practical choice.

90
00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.233
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:34.117 --> 00:07:40.565
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and fronting plus inversion: adjective plus be plus subject.

92
00:07:40.865 --> 00:07:45.224
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

93
00:07:45.524 --> 00:07:47.863
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

94
00:07:48.163 --> 00:07:51.152
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

